I think that it's a Bad Thing to propose the PR as a [efficient]
winning strategy. The PR is, as many other specialized behaviour,
interesting to train some aspects to survive; it's one of a huge
sack full of tactics. Folks who want to be effective should learn
as many of those tactics as possible to become successful in that
difficult game.

In this light, suggesting that you can (should?) always do the PR
and then continue with whatever tactics required to survive is a
misleading and thus bad suggestion. This should be pointed out.

